00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.280
at it. Like I wanted to keep playing.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:07.180
Like I felt like it was like a game that you can learn to be good at.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.460
Um, the only thing that I, that I will say that I do feel like maybe it's just because

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:12.860
I, I needed to get better at it.

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:19.360
But, uh, there was no, it seemed like I had to like run a course a couple of times to like

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:24.260
sort of start to remember where, to like memorize where certain obstacles were before I got to

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.540
them. Definitely too with the refuels.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:31.240
It's like, you have to like really memorize those or else, you know, who knows when the

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:32.260
next one will pop up.

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:36.660
You know, you might run out of fuel if you're, if you're an, you know, an A and B guy.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:37.600
Yeah. Right.

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:44.340
Uh, so I think the difficulty for this game, it's, it's about right with what Sam said,

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:49.120
you know, it's, it's good enough, uh, that at first, you know, you feel kind of good about

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:53.220
the game and, and, and your playing ability, but it challenges you the more you play it.

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:59.000
And I think this is kind of like, this is the first game on the NES that I feel is well

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:03.810
suited for the NES and makes sense why it came to the NES first or the Famicom first before

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:08.270
ever going to arcade, because it really does feel like the kind of game that rewards you

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:13.690
for owning it, sitting down with it, spending the time to get better at the levels.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:15.790
So this way you can get that faster time.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:20.890
I think the one thing that this game is sorely missing is a two player option.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:26.570
I think the fact that like you can't race in real time and that you can only race by time

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:31.370
is something that like, and it's kind of, if you think about it, it's weird because all

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:36.670
the other NES game, not all the other ones will run as that in a second, but most of

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:41.070
the NES games that launch titles were there to showcase the system and be like, here's

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:42.050
what the system can do.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:46.050
And you know, the two controllers and the zapper and stuff like that.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:50.570
And it's like, here we have a game that's really just like, you know, like this one for

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:54.890
you, this one's for you, like you can play this by, you know, and like, well, I feel

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:59.010
like because you're, you could be playing with somebody that doesn't make the same mistakes

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:02.890
as you, um, were there split screen games on the NES?

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:04.710
That's a good question.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.410
