00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:34.690
It's a cool thing. Actually, the reason I did not use it was because I thought that it's just going to be terrible

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.850
because of it, it being on an NES.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.330
I was just focusing on the time trail mode.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.130
Right. Yeah. Which again is the biggest part of the game.

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:48.030
I think like the clunkiness of like not being able to go back, like kind of having to like

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:53.010
think about your course as you're like, like in your head before you're making those like

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:56.210
inputs because you got to think about like longterm what you're putting in.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:59.550
And I think like, it's not, it's not a great creator.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:02.090
I think one, I'm more amazed that it even exists.

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:08.370
